# OPTIONAL — gzip for the HTML pages Django returns (SEO TZ task 11).
#
# Where: /home/autolig1/public_html/.htaccess, ABOVE or BELOW the block that
# cPanel manages:
#     # DO NOT REMOVE. CLOUDLINUX PASSENGER CONFIGURATION BEGIN
#     ...
#     # DO NOT REMOVE. CLOUDLINUX PASSENGER CONFIGURATION END
# Never paste inside that block and never edit its lines: cPanel rewrites it when
# the Python app is restarted / changed in "Setup Python App".
# Make a copy of the file first (cp .htaccess .htaccess.bak-YYYYMMDD).
#
# Everything is inside <IfModule>, so a server without mod_deflate ignores it.
# If the site shows a 500 error after saving, restore the .bak file.
# Preferred alternative: ask Ahost to enable compression at server level (deploy/AHOST_REQUEST.md).

# BEGIN Autoliga compression
<IfModule mod_deflate.c>
    AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/html text/plain text/xml application/xml application/rss+xml application/json
</IfModule>
# END Autoliga compression
